# core/element-detail - Everything asserted about one element.
#
# Answers: every predicate and object on the focus resource, with the graph each
# came from.
#
# Does NOT prove: completeness. What is absent here is absent from the models,
# which is not the same as absent from the enterprise.
#
# Use this to check exact predicate spelling before writing a narrower query. Two
# spellings of a property key are two different predicates, and a join on the
# wrong casing returns fewer rows with no error - so when a result looks
# suspiciously small, come back here and read the real keys for one known element.
#
# Unscoped on purpose: an element's semantic facts, its appearances in views and
# its provenance are in different graphs, and seeing which graph each fact came
# from is most of the value.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT {{GRAPH_VAR:any}} ?predicate ?object
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:any}}
    VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
    ?focus ?predicate ?object .
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY {{GRAPH_VAR:any}} ?predicate ?object
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
